> quite pretty output "eventually", but that uses
> incredibly ugly markup compared to HTML.

*roff is good for plain text output, which was the OP's use case.
HTML can be massaged to do it, but "select all/save as text" is
painful if you have many documents (scripting "links -dump" might
suffice but it's a lot less flexible than *roff).

One of the LinuxDoc or similar SGML/XML markup languages would work,
too.

roff's ugly but works.  e.g. this:
.ce
Nethack info
this is some nethack info,  Hopefully it will be useful!

.ce
Races
.TS
l l r
____
c l r.
Character   alignment   role
D   lawful  Dwarf
@   chaotic Elf
@   any Human
.TE


Renders as:
                        Nethack info
this is some nethack info,  Hopefully it will be useful!

                           Races

Character   alignment    role
----------------------------------
    D       lawful      Dwarf
    @       chaotic       Elf
    @       any         Human


